Report TJERR_FATAL when a fatal error follows a libjpeg warning.

my_emit_message() sets jerr.warning on the first libjpeg warning. One fatal
exit clears it again: my_progress_monitor() sets it to FALSE before its longjmp
when a scan limit is exceeded. Every other fatal exit keeps it. So
tj3GetErrorCode() returns TJERR_WARNING ("non-fatal and recoverable") also
when the call hit a fatal error after the warning (a longjmp from
my_error_exit(), or a THROW) and left the destination buffer unwritten.
Example: a progressive JPEG with junk bytes and then an unsupported SOF5 marker
before the second scan. tj3Decompress8() returns -1, reports TJERR_WARNING, and
writes no rows.

At the bailout label, retval is non-zero only after a fatal exit, so clear the
flag there, as my_progress_monitor() does. TJERR_WARNING then means the call
ran to completion: tj3DecompressHeader() parsed the whole header,
tj3Decompress8() wrote every row. src/runtime/image/codec_jpeg.rs accepts a
decode on that signal. It reads the flag through tj3BunCompletedWithWarning(),
which this patch adds, so a libjpeg-turbo without the patch fails to link.

Upstream has the same sticky flag at 3.2.0 and at main (b33c60b4, 2026-09-18).
There is no upstream issue for it.

--- a/src/turbojpeg.c
+++ b/src/turbojpeg.c
@@ -714,6 +714,18 @@
   return tj3GetErrorCode(handle);
 }
 
+/* bun: whether the last tj3DecompressHeader() or tj3Decompress8() call ran to
+ * completion while libjpeg warned.  The bailout hunks of this patch make the
+ * flag mean that.  src/runtime/image/codec_jpeg.rs calls this instead of
+ * tj3GetErrorCode(), so a build without the patch fails to link. */
+DLLEXPORT int tj3BunCompletedWithWarning(tjhandle handle);
+DLLEXPORT int tj3BunCompletedWithWarning(tjhandle handle)
+{
+  tjinstance *this = (tjinstance *)handle;
+
+  return this && this->jerr.warning;
+}
+
 
 #define SET_PARAM(field, minValue, maxValue) { \
   if (value < minValue || (maxValue > 0 && value > maxValue)) \
@@ -1924,7 +1936,10 @@
     THROW("Invalid data returned in header");
 
 bailout:
-  if (this->jerr.warning) retval = -1;
+  /* bun: as in tj3Decompress8(), a fatal error after a warning must read as
+   * TJERR_FATAL, so that TJERR_WARNING means the header was fully parsed. */
+  if (retval != 0) this->jerr.warning = FALSE;
+  else if (this->jerr.warning) retval = -1;
   return retval;
 }
 
--- a/src/turbojpeg-mp.c
+++ b/src/turbojpeg-mp.c
@@ -287,7 +287,13 @@
 bailout:
   if (dinfo->global_state > DSTATE_START) jpeg_abort_decompress(dinfo);
   free(row_pointer);
-  if (this->jerr.warning) retval = -1;
+  /* bun: the warning flag is sticky, so upstream reports TJERR_WARNING
+   * ("non-fatal and recoverable") from tj3GetErrorCode() even when a fatal
+   * error (longjmp or THROW) followed the warning and left rows of dstBuf
+   * unwritten. retval is non-zero here only on those fatal exits. Clear the
+   * flag for them, so that TJERR_WARNING means every row was written. */
+  if (retval != 0) this->jerr.warning = FALSE;
+  else if (this->jerr.warning) retval = -1;
   return retval;
 }
 
